KeeperExecutorBase::constructor(address registry_)
└── It should initialize with no allowed executor callers (unbound-inert: perform reverts)

KeeperExecutorBase::allowExecutorCaller(address _caller)
├── Given caller is ADMIN_ROLE
│   ├── It should add the caller and emit ExecutorCallerAllowed(_caller)
│   └── Given _caller is address(0)
│       └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorUnauthorizedCaller(address(0))
└── Given caller lacks ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole(ADMIN_ROLE)

KeeperExecutorBase::removeExecutorCaller(address _caller)
├── Given caller is ADMIN_ROLE
│   ├── It should remove the caller and emit ExecutorCallerRemoved(_caller)
│   └── It should return the executor to the unbound-inert state when the set empties
└── Given caller lacks ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole(ADMIN_ROLE)

KeeperExecutorBase::isExecutorCaller(address) / executorCallerCount()
└── It should reflect the allowlist (EnumerableSet semantics: no duplicates)

KeeperExecutorBase::pause() / unpause()
├── It should gate pause to ADMIN or SECURITY, unpause to ADMIN (inherited)
└── It should make perform revert with EnforcedPause while paused
